  "worked_solution": "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get  $a=-2,$ $b=7,$ and $c=1.$",
